gm-method/rendering (a whole GPU subsystem -- terrain/backdrop -- intermittently FAILS to initialize on COLD load while a warm/CLI surface looks fine, 'only parts display'): suspect a SHARED WebGL2 context being POISONED by a transient GL_INVALID_OPERATION error STORM from a DIFFERENT renderer on the same context, not the failing subsystem itself. Witnessed case: an instanced cluster-LOD mesh (multiDrawElements) issued coarse-LOD draw ranges whose start+count*bytesPerIndex exceeded the bound ELEMENT_ARRAY_BUFFER's LIVE GPU size, because the combined index BufferAttribute was not yet GPU-uploaded (three uploads on the render AFTER setIndex) -> ~8000 'glMultiDrawElements: Insufficient buffer size' in one frame -> the concurrent planet GPU init's own GL calls then failed -> its init threw -> a no-op fallback installed, the global it sets never set, no terrain/veg. DECISIVE WITNESS TECHNIQUE: wrap gl.getExtension to hook multiDrawElementsWEBGL/ANGLE and, per call, compare max(offset+count*bpe) vs gl.getBufferParameter(ELEMENT_ARRAY_BUFFER, BUFFER_SIZE) -- count the overruns; a failing cold load showed thousands, a passing load zero. The symptom is INTERMITTENT and COLD-CACHE-biased (first visit = the deployed page), so loop many cache-cleared loads (CDP Network.clearBrowserCache) to reproduce -- a single warm load hides it. TWO-PART FIX: (1) at the symptom source, guard the multiDraw to skip/compact ranges exceeding the live buffer size (a range only over-runs for the pre-upload frame; once uploaded all fit, steady-state unchanged); (2) harden the victim subsystem to survive a transient poisoned context -- drain gl.getError() before its init and RE-ATTEMPT the build once if its ready-global is still unset after settle (the storm is transient; a later clean frame succeeds). For a node_modules/sibling-lib bug, land the guard via a marker-gated idempotent postinstall patch (survives reinstall, no-op once upstream ships it) AND patch the dist copy the static deploy bundles. Distinguish 'failed' from merely 'slow': watch the ready-global up to ~45s -- if it flips late it was slow (widen the wait), if never it failed (fix the cause).